# The buttons voice shows beside Pi. "[NAME] caption" begins a page and
# "LABEL = TEXT" is a button that types TEXT: \r Enter, \e Escape, \t Tab,
# \xHH a byte, \w a wait of 0.4 s. After the text, one of
#   :speak       listen, then type what was said
#   :word        listen, then type it as a search word
#   :paste       a Paste button: type the clipboard, then TEXT; ":paste NAME" then shows a page
#   :page NAME   show another page

# A command begins with \x15, which empties Pi's prompt. No button types into
# a list that Pi has yet to open: voice cannot see when it has, the user can.

[main] Tap Speak and say what Pi should do. The first time: Menu, then OpenRouter key.
Speak = :speak
Send = \r
Stop = \e
Menu = :page menu
Erase = \x15
Up = \e[A
Down = \e[B

[menu] Pi's settings.
Model = \x15/model\r :page pick
Thinking = \x15/thinking\r :page pick
OpenRouter key = \x15/login openrouter\r :page key
New chat = \x15/new\r :page main
Back = :page main

[pick] Say part of a name, or move with the arrows, then Choose.
Say = :word
Up = \e[A
Down = \e[B
Choose = \r :page main
Erase = \x15
Back = \e :page main

[key] When Pi asks how to sign in, tap API key. Then copy your key at openrouter.ai/keys and tap Paste.
API key = \e[B\r
Paste = \r :paste main
Back = \e :page main
